  "description": "Description of development: Phased development comprising (a) the demolition of existing buildings at 202 and 203-208 Blackfriars Road and (b) the erection of a building to accommodate hotel (Use Class C1) with ancillary uses plus refuse stores, plant, cycle parking and hard and soft landscaping and associated works.\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tSummary of proposed development for consultation purposes: \r\r> Hotel accommodation with 307 rooms, including 5% fully wheelchair accessible rooms and a further 5% available to be adapted as wheelchair accessible rooms. \r>  A height of 85.33m AOD (23 storeys) with two lower shoulders at 61.18m AOD (17 storeys). \r>  Layout featuring: \r - Basement: Back of house and plant. \r - Ground floor: Public areas, including a pantry, café, guest laundry and reception area \r - Mezzanine: Co-working café, and back of house areas. \r - First Floor: Staff back of house areas, bedrooms and gym. \r - Second floor and above: Hotel rooms.\r> Servicing is proposed via Scoresby Street. Additional entrances and activity to street are also proposed on Blackfriars Road and Dolben Street.  \r> 313 sqm GIA of ancillary space is proposed, including a reception/lounge/bar/co-working cafe space on the ground floor and mezzanine which will be open to the public. This includes a unit on the ground floor operated by as a pantry shop by the hotel. \r> The building line has been set back at ground floor along Blackfriars Road using a cantilever to enhance and create public space. \r",
